#!/bin/sh
# hidex-uninstall [--yes] (hidex --uninstall): removes hIDEx and everything it brought, after saying what and
# asking: its sessions (ended, their running commands stopped), its versions and tools (~/.local/share/hidex),
# ~/.local/bin/hidex, what it kept per project (~/.local/state/hidex), its sessions' state, its entries in
# zellij's plugin permissions, and the PATH line install.sh added to ~/.bashrc or ~/.zshrc. Left as they are:
# your projects, and zellij's own "don't show the setup wizard again" choice.
# HIDEX_PREFIX: when installed elsewhere than ~/.local.
prefix=${HIDEX_PREFIX:-$HOME/.local}
root=$prefix/share/hidex
run=${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/run/user/$(id -u)}/hidex
state=${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/hidex
perms=${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/zellij/permissions.kdl

if [ -n "${ZELLIJ_SESSION_NAME:-}" ] && [ -d "$run/$ZELLIJ_SESSION_NAME" ]; then
  echo "hIDEx: quit hIDEx first (Alt+q), then run hidex --uninstall from a plain terminal"; exit 1
fi

# the sessions: one state folder each, its zellij reached through its "current" link
sessions=$(for d in "$run"/*/current; do [ -e "$d" ] && basename "$(dirname "$d")"; done)
# the files install.sh may have put its PATH line in (fish: a file of its own)
fish=${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/fish/conf.d/hidex.fish
rcs=$(for f in "$HOME/.bashrc" "${ZDOTDIR:-$HOME}/.zshrc" "$HOME/.zshrc" "$HOME/.profile" "$fish"; do
  [ ! -L "$f" ] && grep -qs "# hIDEx$" "$f" && echo "$f"; done | sort -u)

echo "This removes hIDEx:"
[ -n "$sessions" ] && echo "  its sessions, ended now (commands still running in them are stopped): $(echo $sessions)"
echo "  $root (every version and tool, $(du -sh "$root" 2>/dev/null | cut -f1))"
echo "  $prefix/bin/hidex"
[ -d "$state" ] && echo "  $state (themes and Python kept per project)"
[ -n "$rcs" ] && echo "  the PATH line it added in: $(echo $rcs)"
if [ "${1:-}" != --yes ]; then
  printf 'Remove? [y/N] '
  read -r answer
  [ "$answer" = y ] || { echo "Nothing removed."; exit 0; }
fi

for n in $sessions; do
  z=$run/$n/current/tools/bin/zellij
  [ -x "$z" ] || z=zellij
  env -u ZELLIJ_SESSION_NAME "$z" kill-session "$n" >/dev/null 2>&1
  env -u ZELLIJ_SESSION_NAME "$z" delete-session --force "$n" >/dev/null 2>&1
done
rm -rf "$run" "$state" "$prefix/bin/hidex" "$root"
# zellij's permissions: the entries of hIDEx's plugin (by its file name)
if [ -f "$perms" ]; then
  awk '/^"[^"]*hidex-panes[^"]*\.wasm" \{/ { skip = 1; next } skip && /^\}/ { skip = 0; next } !skip' "$perms" > "$perms.new" &&
    mv "$perms.new" "$perms"
fi
for f in $rcs; do if [ "$f" = "$fish" ]; then rm -f "$f"; else sed -i "/# hIDEx$/d" "$f"; fi; done
echo "hIDEx removed."
